*************------- Annual Sector Performance Report (ASPR) 2024  ---------------************

The Annual Sector Performance Report (ASPR) 2024 is the Government of Bangladesh's flagship annual sector report for monitoring the performance of the primary education subsector. Prepared by the Directorate of Primary Education (DPE) with technical support from UNICEF, the report assesses sector progress against the Fourth Primary Education Development Programme (PEDP4), national education priorities, and Sustainable Development Goal 4 (SDG 4). It consolidates evidence from administrative data, financial records, learning assessments, and sector-wide monitoring to support evidence-based planning, policy formulation, and resource allocation.

##### My Role

As the **Education Data Collection and Analysis Expert (Consultant)**, I led the technical analysis, validation, and reporting of education sector performance indicators. My work involved integrating data from multiple sources, conducting statistical and financial analyses, preparing analytical outputs, and contributing to the development of the ASPR 2024.

##### Key Contributions

##### Education Sector Performance Analysis

* Analyzed national progress against the PEDP4 Results Framework and annual operational targets.
* Assessed trends in access, participation, equity, efficiency, quality, governance, and resource utilization across the primary education sector.
* Conducted comparative analyses using historical administrative data to identify sector achievements, emerging challenges, and priority intervention areas.
* Prepared statistical summaries and analytical narratives for inclusion in the Annual Sector Performance Report.

##### Education Indicator Computation

Calculated and validated key education indicators, including:
* Gross Intake Rate (GIR)
* Net Intake Rate (NIR)
* Gross Enrolment Ratio (GER)
* Net Enrolment Ratio (NER)
* Promotion, repetition, and dropout rates
* Survival and completion rates
* Internal efficiency indicators using the UNESCO Reconstructed Cohort Method
* Gender Parity Index (GPI)
* Student–Teacher Ratio (STR)
* Student–Classroom Ratio (SCR)
* Pre-primary education indicators
* Teacher qualification and deployment statistics
* School infrastructure, WASH, electricity, ICT, and accessibility indicators

##### Financial and Resource Analysis

* Analyzed public expenditure on primary education using Ministry of Primary and Mass Education (MoPME) budget data, National GDP data, and other forms of budget and financial data.
* Assessed annual budget allocation, expenditure trends, and utilization rates.
* Estimated per-child public expenditure and examined financing trends over time.
* Analyzed the share of education expenditure within the national budget and GDP.
* Produced statistical tables and visualizations to support financial reporting and sector analysis.

##### Data Management and Quality Assurance

* Integrated data from multiple administrative sources, including APSS, APSC, IPEMIS, and financial datasets.
* Performed comprehensive data cleaning, consistency checks, missing-value analysis, and validation before statistical analysis.
* Conducted historical trend validation to ensure consistency with previous ASPR editions.
* Verified indicator calculations against UNESCO-UIS methodologies and national reporting standards.

